title: Veeam: Jobs Backup
agents: windows
catalog: os/storage
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors the status of the backups jobs run by the Veeam
 backup tool. In order to carry out the check, the Veeam agent plugin
 needs to be installed on the backup server. See special instructions in the
 comment section of the two Veeam agent plug-in scripts on how to install
 the scripts.

 This check is {OK} if the result of the backup is Success. It is {WARN} if the
 result of the backup is Warning. It is {CRIT} if the result of the backup is
 Failed.

 If the result of the backup is None, the state of the job decides. While the
 job is running, the previous result is kept. If the job is not running, it has
 no execution history yet and the check is {OK}. Any state that cannot be
 interpreted results in {UNKNOWN}.

 For backup policies managed by the Veeam Agent, the result of the policy only
 reflects applying the policy to the protected computers. Therefore, the last
 finished backup of each computer currently protected by the policy is evaluated
 in the same way, and the service shows the worst of them. If more than three
 computers have problems, their number is shown and they are listed in the
 details. Computers without problems and computers without a finished backup
 yet are listed in the details. If the protected computers cannot be
 determined, the service is {UNKNOWN}. This requires the current version of the
 agent plug-in.

discovery:
 One service is created for each backup job created by the Veeam tool.

item:
 The name of the backup job.
